# Line-ending policy for the published artifact.
#
# Mirrors the source repository's .gitattributes, kept to the rules that apply
# to this tree (it ships no .githooks/ and no tools/openapi/ snapshot).
#
# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true by default, so without this
# file every shell script would be checked out with CRLF. A trailing \r turns
# `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` into an invalid interpreter path and breaks every
# line end, so `bash setup.sh` fails on Linux with errors like
# `$'\r': command not found`. Force LF regardless of the user's core.autocrlf.
*.sh text eol=lf

# pnpm patch files are applied by diff context matching. A CRLF checkout
# changes every line of the payload, so `pnpm install` fails to apply the
# patches referenced from frontend/pnpm-workspace.yaml (patchedDependencies).
# The source repository stores them as LF; pin that here so the checked-out
# bytes stay appliable regardless of the user's core.autocrlf.
*.patch text eol=lf

# cmd.exe parses .bat/.cmd labels (goto / call :label) by seeking through the
# file; with LF-only line endings it mis-locates labels and jumps into the
# wrong branch (seen: build_frontend.bat --no-pause landing in :opt_mirror).
# Force CRLF on checkout regardless of the user's core.autocrlf setting.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
